course: dictionary
lesson: 2038
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so the context tells you which one to use. «Conglomerate is a rock made of rounded pebbles, rolled smooth by rivers or waves, cemented together.» The clues are rounded pebbles, rolled smooth and cemented together, so a conglomerate is made of many different stones stuck into one lump.
explain: The same word can mean something else in another subject. A conglomerate can also be a big company that owns many different businesses, or simply a mass of different things gathered together. Read the words around it to decide which meaning fits.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does «a rock made of many different stones stuck together» still make sense? If it does, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Conglomerate is a noun, and it can also be used as an adjective, as in a conglomerate company.
fact: In science, a conglomerate is a rock made of rounded pebbles and stones stuck together by finer material, like natural concrete.
fact: The rounded pebbles show that they were once rolled by rivers or the sea.
fact: In business, a conglomerate is a big company made up of many different businesses that sell different things.
fact: A mass of different things gathered together can also be called a conglomerate.
exercise: «Conglomerate is a rock made of rounded pebbles, rolled smooth by rivers or waves, cemented together.» What do the pebbles look like? | Sharp and jagged | Made of gold | Hot from a fire | *Rounded and smooth, rolled by water
exercise: A company that owns many different businesses is called a conglomerate. What does this tell you? | *It owns many different businesses that sell different things | It is a small family shop | It is a type of pebble | It sells only one kind of shoe
exercise: «Conglomerate is a rock made of rounded pebbles, rolled smooth by rivers or waves, cemented together.» What does cemented mean here? | Washed away by the sea | *Stuck firmly together | Broken into dust | Painted bright colours
test: Nadia says conglomerate can mean a big company. Is she right? | No, it only means a small pebble | *Yes, it can mean a big company made of many different businesses | No, it only means a kind of cake | No, it only means a grey cloud
test: A conglomerate rock is like natural concrete. What holds its pebbles together? | Glue from a shop | Water only | *Finer material that sticks them together | Nothing at all
exam: Which sentence uses conglomerate to mean a mass of different things? | *The heap of toys, books and socks on the floor was a conglomerate of different things | The sea wall was made of old bricks | The rock was grey and very hard | The pebbles were rolled smooth by the waves
